war|REVIEW: [GRAMMAR] Armed fighting is a single source-supported noun boundary; particular-war versus warfare countability is not artificially split. Translation preserves town and daily-life scope. grammarNotesEn ends with an internal proposal comment, which should be removed by an exact-parent overlay before effective review.
appreciate|PASS: Value/gratitude and understanding-importance are separated according to the two Oxford groups. Patience translates naturally as trân trọng; how much skill retains the degree construction. Accessible Cambridge text supports noun/-ing/that/how complements. No intransitive financial meaning is smuggled into these transitive drafts.
gallon|PASS: Countable volume unit and US-labelled container avoid conflating imperial and US measures. Accessible Cambridge search text confirms different sizes. No copied conversion example or unverified exact conversion enters the content; ga-lông names the unit rather than a container type.
injure|PASS: Shoulder injury and gravel fall retain the physical sense and causal situation. Vietnamese bị thương is natural for the self-injury construction. Grammar covers a person, body part and reflexive object; no emotional hurt sense is asserted.
painting|PASS: A countable harbour picture, uncountable artistic practice and uncountable fence-coating work represent all three ordinals without overlap. Vietnamese separately uses bức tranh, vẽ tranh and sơn. Examples preserve dawn, relaxation and unexpected duration; noun countability notes fit each boundary.
